values ('f2a3b4c5-6d7e-4f77-8a77-8b9c0d1e2f07', 'survey-of-spanish-peninsular-literature', 'Survey of Spanish (Peninsular) Literature', 'Students identify major periods, genres, authors, debates, and cultural contexts in Peninsular Spanish literary history, and analyze literary form, language, genre, and narrative or poetic technique in Spanish with historically grounded close reading. They explain how Iberian multilingualism, religion, empire, class, gender, region, war, dictatorship, democracy, and memory shape literary production, connect canonical texts to canon formation and marginalized voices, and support an original historical-literary argument in writing and oral presentation.');

